:: Outside [nobr]
<<CurrentObjective>>
<<HUD>>

<<if not $leftApartmentOnce>>
<div class="prose-block">
<p>I lock the door behind me. The hallway smells like someone else&apos;s breakfast. Something good. Something real. My stomach tightens, whether or not I&apos;ve eaten.</p>
</div>
<<set $leftApartmentOnce to true>>
<</if>>

<<if $novaCureDay1Done and not $seenWalkHomeD1>>
<<ImagePlaceholder "Walking home past a bar, a whistle, a hand around her keys" "banner" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/walk-home-whistle.png">>
<div class="prose-block">
<p>The walk home from the bus stop takes seven minutes. It used to take five. Shorter legs. Shorter stride. My hips sway with each step   I&apos;m not doing it on purpose. It&apos;s how this skeleton moves.</p>
<p>I pass a group of men outside a bar. Four of them. Beers in hand. I don&apos;t look at them. I look at the sidewalk. My hood is up. My hands are in my pockets.</p>
<p>A whistle. Sharp, two-toned, the universal sound of a man reducing a woman to her outline.</p>
<p>I walk faster. My heart hammers. My keys are in my pocket   I pull them out, hold one between my fingers, a weapon I didn&apos;t know I&apos;d need until this exact second. This is what women do. This is what women have always done. I never thought about it. Not once. Not in twenty years of being the species that whistles.</p>
</div>
<<set $seenWalkHomeD1 to true>>
<</if>>

<<if $day is 2 and $d02BoughtClothes and not $seenCatcallD2>>
<<ImagePlaceholder "Walking past a construction site, hood up, bag in hand" "banner" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/catcall-street.png">>
<div class="prose-block">
<p>I&apos;m walking with a plastic bag full of women&apos;s clothes. My first women&apos;s clothes. Purchased with my money, from a store three blocks from the apartment I&apos;ve lived in for eight months, and until two days ago, I would have walked right past the women&apos;s section without a second thought. Now I&apos;m carrying it like it&apos;s contraband.</p>
<p>Hood still up. Head down. The bag rustles against my leg with every step.</p>
<p>I pass a construction site. Chain-link fence. Two workers on a break   one sitting on a cooler, one leaning against a truck.</p>
<p>&quot;Hey gorgeous, smile for me!&quot;</p>
<p>Loud. Directed at me. The voice comes from the guy on the cooler. He&apos;s grinning. Like he just said something charming. Like &quot;hey gorgeous, smile for me&quot; is a gift he&apos;s bestowing.</p>
<p>I freeze mid-step. My whole body locks. I don&apos;t turn. I don&apos;t respond. I don&apos;t make eye contact. I walk faster. My keys are already in my pocket. I close my hand around them, a sharp metal fang between my fingers.</p>
<p>The second worker: &quot;Leave her alone, man.&quot; Then, to me: &quot;Sorry about him.&quot;</p>
<p>I don&apos;t stop. I keep walking. Heart pounding, face hot, a cocktail of emotions I can&apos;t separate   violation, anger, and something I don&apos;t want to name. Something that recognizes: he saw a woman. Without me performing it. Without me trying. Without me doing a single thing other than existing on a sidewalk with a bag of clothes.</p>
<p>The world is gendering me correctly and I have feelings about that and I don&apos;t know what any of them are.</p>
<p>Past the catcall. Heart still hammering. Keys in my fist. I pass a hair salon   a woman in the chair getting her hair blow-dried, scrolling her phone, bored, comfortable. I&apos;ve never been in a hair salon. As Aiden, I went to a barber. Not today. Today I walked to a thrift store and bought panties and survived a catcall and that&apos;s more than enough for one Saturday.</p>
</div>
<<set $seenCatcallD2 to true>>
<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress + 5, 0, 100)>>
<<set $player.fem to Math.clamp($player.fem + 1, 0, 100)>>
<</if>>

